 rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "The open Texas 23rd seat, vacated by Tony Gonzales, leans Republican by about seven points on partisanship, and most expert raters call the race Likely R, with a couple moving to Lean R or Tossup. Republican nominee Brandon Herrera has outraised Democrat Katy Padilla Stout substantially, but he has also drawn heavy outside opposition spending and a stream of unflattering coverage over crude and extremist remarks, with national Democrats targeting the border district.\n\nPolling is sparse and dated: a March Democratic-sponsored survey showed only a two-point Republican edge, and prediction markets put the Democrat's chances near 40 percent. The forecast lands at a modest Republican margin of about three points, with wide uncertainty given the thin data and the volatility of the nominee's controversies.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2506, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.355, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3283, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.203, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2999, "margin": -3.0}]}